course: dictionary
lesson: 12854
title: Enforced: rules and choices
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enforced has two meanings. The first is made to be obeyed. Rules and laws are enforced by people with power, such as police, referees or teachers. «The speed limit is strictly enforced by cameras.» The rule must be obeyed, and the cameras check that it is.
explain: The second meaning is about choice. Something enforced is forced on you, so you did not pick it. «Mia had an enforced rest after her operation.» Mia did not want to stay in bed; she had no choice.
explain: To decide which meaning fits, look at the context. Is someone making a rule happen, or is someone stuck with something they did not choose? Then swap in the word «forced» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Enforced means made to happen, or made to be obeyed by people with power.
fact: Enforced is also the past form of the verb enforce: enforce, enforces, enforced, enforcing.
fact: Police, referees and teachers often enforce rules.
fact: «An enforced break» means a break that you had no choice about.
fact: «Strictly enforced» means a rule is checked and followed very carefully.
exercise: «The speed limit is strictly enforced by cameras.» What does enforced mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Forgotten by everyone | *Made to be obeyed | Made from a soft material
exercise: «Mia had an enforced rest after her operation.» What does enforced suggest? | Mia chose to rest for fun | *Mia had no choice | Mia was very happy | Mia was too tired to read
exercise: «The referee enforced the rule and gave a free kick.» Which word is a form of the verb enforce? | free | rule | *enforced | referee
test: «The school rules are enforced by teachers.» Who enforces the rules? | Nobody at all | Birds | *Teachers | The weather
test: «Ben was given an enforced break from football after his injury.» What does enforced mean? | Very fast | *Forced on him, not chosen | Shared with all his friends | Chosen by Ben for fun
exam: «The ferry was cancelled, so Lily had an enforced stay in the town for two nights.» What does enforced mean here? | Shared with her friends | Enjoyed very much | *Forced on her, not chosen | Made to be obeyed by the ferry company
